# 14. DAILY / WEEKLY MENTOR APPROVAL SETTINGS

Provide a separate Approval Mode setting.

Options:

1. Daily Approval.
2. Weekly Approval.

The Entry Mode and Approval Mode must work independently.

All four combinations must be implemented.

## 14.1 Daily Entry + Daily Approval

1. Student enters today's activities.
2. Student submits the daily report.
3. Mentor reviews periods individually.
4. Mentor approves the periods.
5. The day becomes approved only when all required periods are approved.
6. The next scheduled reporting day unlocks.

## 14.2 Daily Entry + Weekly Approval

1. Student enters activities separately for each day.
2. Daily reports can be saved as drafts.
3. The system collects those entries into the weekly reporting unit.
4. The student submits the completed week.
5. Mentor reviews periods individually.
6. The full week becomes approved when all required periods are approved.
7. The next reporting week unlocks.

## 14.3 Weekly Entry + Daily Approval

1. Student sees all days in one weekly interface.
2. The system allows entry into the appropriate reporting day.
3. Each day has a separate submission unit.
4. Mentor approves every required period of that day.
5. The next scheduled day unlocks only after the previous day is approved.

The weekly interface must not bypass daily approval restrictions.

## 14.4 Weekly Entry + Weekly Approval

1. Student sees the complete weekly reporting interface.
2. Student records activities for all scheduled days.
3. Student submits the weekly report.
4. Mentor examines periods individually.
5. The weekly report becomes approved when all required periods are approved.
6. The next reporting week unlocks.

## 14.5 CRITICAL REPORTING IMPLEMENTATION RULE

Do not confuse:

- Entry Mode.
- Approval Mode.
- Reporting Submission Unit.

Entry Mode controls how the student sees and enters information.

Approval Mode controls the boundary at which the mentor must approve the work.

Use the following logic:

- Daily Approval = one approval unit per scheduled day.
- Weekly Approval = one approval unit per reporting week.

In Daily Entry + Weekly Approval, keep the daily inputs inside one weekly approval unit.

In Weekly Entry + Daily Approval, keep separate daily approval units inside the weekly interface.

Store both Entry Mode and Approval Mode as snapshots when a new reporting unit is created, so later setting changes cannot corrupt historical workflows.

## 14.6 Sequential Locking

Implement a proper backend validation for reporting progression.

Daily Approval:

The next scheduled reporting day is locked until the previous scheduled day is fully approved.

Weekly Approval:

The next reporting week is locked until the previous week's reporting unit is fully approved.

The first reporting unit of the academic year must not require a previous approval.

Ignore weekends, college holidays, and authorized cancelled periods.

Do not rely only on disabled buttons in the frontend.

The backend must reject unauthorized submissions.

## 14.7 Settings Changes

Admin can change Entry Mode and Approval Mode independently.

Warn the administrator before changing settings when drafts or pending reports exist.

New settings should normally apply to future reporting units.

Existing submitted reports must retain their original reporting rules.

Do not automatically delete, merge, or rewrite existing report data.

